  "result": "I fixed the duplicate-delivery bug in `src/lib/event-bus.ts`. The event-bus unit tests pass (9/9). I didn't run the service-level suites.\n\n**Cause:** `subscribe()` is copy-on-write, so each subscribe replaces the set for that event type with a new one. The unsubscribe it returned deleted from the set captured at subscribe time, which can be stale. When a later handler had subscribed, a detach removed nothing live, so the handler stayed attached. Each detach/re-attach cycle left another copy behind. That is why webhooks, audit rows and the usage counter multiplied, while notifications were not affected. Notification fan-out subscribes once at module load and is never detached.\n\n**Fix:** The unsubscribe now looks up the set currently published for that type and publishes a new set without the handler. Calling it after the handler is already gone is a no-op. The existing `registerEventHandlers()` guard already makes a second registration without a detach a no-op, so I left it unchanged.",
